For the target arm \(a=1\) in SDC mode, let \(\mathcal I_{BK}^{\rho,s}\) be the union over \(b\in\{-1,+1\}\) of the intervals whose lower and upper endpoints are obtained from \(\text{def:cone-duals}\) after evaluating all cell quantities under \(P^{\rho,s}\) and replacing the unrestricted domain \(\mathbb R_+^2\) by \(\Lambda_1\); explicitly,
\[
\mathcal I_{BK}^{\rho,s}
=\bigcup_{b\in\{-1,+1\}}
\left[
\sup_{\lambda\in\Lambda_1}\left\{c_1-b\lambda'h_1^{\mathrm{SDC}}
+\sum_{j\in\mathcal M_1}p_j\min_{v\in[0,1]}(1-b\lambda's_j^{\mathrm{SDC}})v\right\},
\inf_{\lambda\in\Lambda_1}\left\{c_1+b\lambda'h_1^{\mathrm{SDC}}
+\sum_{j\in\mathcal M_1}p_j\max_{v\in[0,1]}(1+b\lambda's_j^{\mathrm{SDC}})v\right\}
\right].
\]
All quantities inside the braces are evaluated under \(P^{\rho,s}\).
